    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.78) and **Masyn Winn** (64.02) anchor our offensive production. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a high-leverage lineup spot batting second against McGreevy, while **Masyn Winn** draws the most favorable matchup of the day against Kelly, whose 5.29 xERA suggests we should see high run-scoring potential. **Tyler Freeman** (65.30) also emerges as a surprisingly strong play; despite batting eighth, he benefits from a 14% park-factor boost that elevates his ceiling against Singer. These three represent our primary vehicles for capitalizing on stolen base opportunities, which remain the focal point of our strategy to climb the roto standings.\n\nOn the bench, **Jonathan Aranda** (46.16) proved to be the most difficult exclusion, narrowly missing the cut due to his platoon disadvantage against Rivera. While his underlying xwOBA of 0.372 is encouraging, the efficiency models favor the current starters\u2014specifically **Dylan Beavers** (57.72)\u2014who receive a clearer boost from their respective platoon alignments. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Arraez** (46.36); although he occupies a premium leadoff spot, his score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against an elite arm in Miller (2.85 xERA). We will keep **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Jonathan Aranda** ready as potential pinch-hit options should the game scripts shift or if any late-breaking lineup changes occur for **Cal Raleigh** or **Taylor Ward**.\n\nWe continue to manage our volume carefully, keeping **Daulton Varsho** (55.75) and **JJ Bleday** (52.74) in the mix despite marginal scores, as we must balance daily efficiency with total game caps. **Cal Raleigh** (52.90) and **Taylor Ward** (53.23) are hovering just above our marginal threshold; both are high-variance starts, but their projected plate appearance volume against mid-rotation arms like Roupp and Lambert justifies their inclusion over deeper bench options like **Drew Gilbert**, who remains below our mandatory 40.0 efficiency floor. There are no immediate weather threats to report, so we are proceeding with this configuration to maximize our 5x5 categorical output.",
